 "final_summary": "The bug was in the sorting logic where a leading '-' in the sort parameter was incorrectly interpreted as ascending order. The fix ensures that when a sort field starts with '-', the direction is correctly set to 'DESC' and the '-' is stripped from the field. This ensures that '-priority' sorts tasks by priority in descending order. The fix has been verified with both the reproduction test and the full test suite.",
 "diff": "diff --git a/tracker/query.py b/tracker/query.py\nindex 3166a82..adb1026 100644\n--- a/tracker/query.py\n+++ b/tracker/query.py\n@@ -19,10 +19,11 @@ def parse_sort(value):\n         part = raw.strip()\n         if not part:\n             continue\n-        direction = \"ASC\"\n-        if part.startswith(\"-\"):\n-            direction = \"ASC\"\n+        if part.startswith('-'):\n+            direction = \"DESC\"\n             part = part[1:]\n+        else:\n+            direction = \"ASC\"\n         if part not in SORTABLE_FIELDS:\n             raise ValidationError(f\"cannot sort by {part}\", {\"sort\": \"invalid\"})\n         order.append((part, direction))\n",
